codex
The Python implementation now translates to a single return expression in the supported AST subset. For the proof, I’m separating two obligations: loading the exact translated function binds the expected closure, and invoking that closure on an arbitrary symbolic character-code sequence returns the cardinality of the deduplicated lowercase sequence. Together they cover definition loading and functional behavior.
